# secret-lint allowlist. Format: <regex>\t<reason>
# An entry WITHOUT a reason is itself a finding — an unexplained allowlist is
# how a real credential gets waved through months later.
scripts/secret-lint\.mjs	the scanner's own detection regexes; it must contain the shapes it detects
tests/secret-lint\.negative\.test\.mjs	the scanner's negative proof; its fixtures are assembled from harmless parts at runtime

tests/claims\.test\.cjs	the secret-detection CLAIM test; AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE is AWS's published documentation example key and the input that proves SecretDetector fires
tests/telemetry-default\.test\.cjs	runtime telemetry proof; contains no credential material, listed so a future key-shaped fixture there is a deliberate decision
